> A hand-checkable log-mean-exp and its gradient

Shift each column by its stopped maximum m before exponentiating:
logmeanexp(ell)=m+log(sum exp(ell−m))−log K.
For log weights log(1), log(2), log(3), the bound is log(2), normalized weights are
(1/6,2/6,3/6), and effective sample size is 1/sum(w²)=18/7≈2.57143.
The derivative of the **negative** bound with respect to ell_k is −w_k. These same weights
arise by differentiating the original objective; the computation keeps the full ordinary path.
Equal weights give ESS=K; one dominant weight approaches ESS=1. This diagnoses concentration
among supplied draws, not the accuracy of the likelihood estimate or a training convergence proof.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/iwae_hand.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  namespace n     = dm::nn;
  namespace m     = n::models;
  const auto t    = n::DType::Float64;
  auto       logw = n::tensor({0., std::log(2.), std::log(3.)}, {3, 1}, t).requires_grad_();
  const auto b    = m::IwaeLogMeanExp(logw);
  const auto g    = n::grad(-n::sum(b), {logw})[0];
  auto       o    = m::ImportanceWeightedBound(
      n::zeros({3, 1}, t), n::zeros({3, 1}, t), n::zeros({3, 1}, t), -logw.reshape({3}), 3);
  if (std::abs(b.item() - std::log(2.)) > 1e-14 ||
      std::abs(o.effective_samples.item() - 18. / 7) > 1e-14)
    return 1;
  auto plot = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  plot.title("Three importance weights / ESS = 18/7")
      .x_label("sample index")
      .y_label("normalized weight / negative derivative");
  std::vector<double> index{1, 2, 3};
  plot.lines(
      index,
      o.normalized_weights.to_vector<double>(),
      "normalized weight",
      dm::RGBA{37, 99, 235},
      2);
  plot.lines(index, g.to_vector<double>(), "negative-bound derivative", dm::RGBA{220, 38, 38}, 2);
  plot.save_svg("build/iwae_hand.svg");
  std::print(
      "Bound {:.12f}; negative bound {:.12f}; ESS {:.12f}.\n",
      b.item(),
      o.loss.item(),
      o.effective_samples.item());
  const auto extreme = m::IwaeLogMeanExp(n::tensor({1000., 1001., 999.}, {3, 1}, t));
  if (!std::isfinite(extreme.item()))
    return 1;
  std::print("Shifted extreme bound {:.12f}; no raw exp(1000).\n", extreme.item());
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
Bound 0.693147180560; negative bound -0.693147180560; ESS 2.571428571429.
Shifted extreme bound 1000.308993675776; no raw exp(1000).
\image(figures/iwae_hand.svg)
// result_end

\caption(The objective's normalized partials have the opposite sign of its importance weights. The sum of those negative partials is −1 for one image.)
\alttext(Three positive normalized weights 1/6, 2/6 and 3/6 and their negative bound derivatives share the same plot.)

Jensen's inequality bounds log p(x) by the **expected** log importance estimate under
independent q draws. Expected IWAE bounds tighten as K increases under the usual integrability
conditions. A specific finite draw is not guaranteed to improve: extending log weights[0]
with −10 lowers logmeanexp from 0 to approximately −0.693102. All comparisons below retain
finite estimates rather than presenting them as exact log likelihoods.

> Native data preparation and visible paired fitting

The offline native beta-vae-assets preparation exhausts 2 shapes×3 sizes×7 x×7 y=294 unique
binary 28×28 images. Radius is size+2, center=(3x+5,3y+5); circles and squares use inclusive
Euclidean/Chebyshev radii. Residue(x+2y+size+3shape) mod7 assigns test0, validation1, fit2–6,
yielding 210/42/42 disjoint combinations with balanced factor marginals. Factors are used only
in post-training fitting-only probes. This is a tiny structured teaching lattice, not an IID
benchmark or evidence of disentanglement.

```{cpp, results="markdown", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build/iwae");
  const std::filesystem::path cache = dm::datasets::data_home();
  dm::datasets::prepare_example_data("beta-vae-assets", cache.string());
  auto                       arrays = n::load_npz((cache / "beta_vae/factors.npz").string());
  std::set<int>              ids;
  std::set<std::vector<int>> images;
  for (auto& [name, value] : arrays) {
    if (name.ends_with("_images")) {
      for (int b = 0; b < value.size(0); ++b) {
        auto row = n::select(value, 0, b).to_vector<int>();
        if (!images.insert(row).second)
          return 1;
      }
      value = n::cast(value, n::DType::Float32);
    }
    if (name.ends_with("_source_ids"))
      for (int id : value.to_vector<int>())
        if (!ids.insert(id).second)
          return 1;
  }
  if (ids.size() != 294 || images.size() != 294)
    return 1;
  n::save_npz("build/iwae/data.npz", arrays);
  std::filesystem::copy_file(
      cache / "beta_vae/manifest.json",
      "build/iwae/data_manifest.json",
      std::filesystem::copy_options::overwrite_existing);
  std::print(
      "| split | images | features |\n|---|---:|---:|\n| fit |210|784|\n| validation |42|784|\n| "
      "test |42|784|\n");
}
