> Reproduction evidence and API boundary

All 34 source archives are compared by dtype, shape and every value byte: algebra, data,
Gaussian banks, shared initialization, first gradients/Adam updates, every eligible checkpoint,
selected endpoints, all three nested test estimates, prior codes/probabilities and factor probes.
Both full histories and batch/source order match exactly. An optional NumPy oracle independently
checks all first parameter derivatives, exact first Adam updates, sampled Gaussian densities,
normalized weights/ESS, every saved decoder draw and all six common validation scores.
It neither fits models nor prepares/downloads data.

```
python3 scripts/check_importance_weighted_autoencoder.py docs/mepml/examples/nn/2_autoencoders/2.2_variational_autoencoders/build/iwae --json build/nn-report-conversion/importance_vae/oracle.json
```

Native operations are IwaeLogMeanExp, ImportanceWeightedBound and ImportanceWeightedAutoencoder,
with GaussianVaeDecode for final-code-only logits. The same functions are exposed in Python/R;
all five bound and eleven forward fields own lifetime. Host tests exercise Float64, explicit
caller-owned Adam, input/noise gradients and collection safety. This reusable API/report
conversion does not mark unfinished independent Python/R experiment loops as complete ports.
